{
  "manifestVersion": "2026.10.22-1",
  "notes": "Every artifact Stillsong downloads at first run, pinned by exact URL + size + sha256 — models, runtimes, the CPython build, uv, and every Python wheel (python.wheels, generated by scripts/lock-python.mjs; never edit that section by hand). Setup fetches exactly these blobs with the Rust downloader and installs the Python environment offline from the verified wheelhouse; no resolver ever runs on a user's machine. The one exception is the GitHub-generated ComfyUI source tarball: GitHub keeps the contents of a commit archive stable but may regenerate the compressed bytes (it did in January 2023), which would fail a byte hash on every shipped release at once, so that item carries treeSha256 — the digest of the extracted files (node scripts/tree-digest.mjs <tar.gz>, mirrored by tree_sha256 in src-tauri/src/components.rs) — and its size is nominal (the downloader accepts up to twice it). Never weaken either check. allowedHosts is where a download may START: every pinned URL must be https on one of these hosts (a leading '*.' entry would match subdomains). Redirects issued by those hosts are followed to any https URL — CDN hostnames change between releases and the app never updates itself, so pinning them would only break setup; the pinned size + sha256 is what guarantees the bytes, whichever host serves them.",
  "allowedHosts": [
    "huggingface.co",
    "github.com",
    "files.pythonhosted.org",
    "download-r2.pytorch.org"
  ],
  "python": {
    "version": "3.12.15",
    "notes": "Exact interpreter (the python-dist item below) and the wheel set resolved once at release time from ComfyUI's pinned requirements.txt. `constraints` is hand-maintained: it holds the versions this stack was validated on wherever ComfyUI leaves a requirement open (torch is the one that matters for bit-identical codes). `exclude` is hand-maintained too: packages ComfyUI's requirements resolve but Stillsong deliberately does not ship — today the workflow-template media bundles (sample images/videos for the web frontend's template gallery, which a headless ComfyUI never serves; their absence only disables the /templates route with one logged error at boot). The lock script drops them after resolution and refuses a name the resolution does not contain. Regenerate everything below with `npm run lock:python` after every ComfyUI bump or constraint/exclude change (`--freeze` keeps every other pin where it is).",
    "constraints": [
      "torch==2.13.0+cu130"
    ],
    "exclude": [
      "comfyui-workflow-templates-media-api",
      "comfyui-workflow-templates-media-video",
      "comfyui-workflow-templates-media-image",
      "comfyui-workflow-templates-media-other",
      "comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-01",
      "comfyui-workflow-templates-media-assets-02"
    ],
    "lockedAt": "2026-10-22",
    "lockedWith": "uv 0.13.1",
    "requirementsSha256": "cd4ac76294534ac751816903d79c860d8b6a55ef89fcd50bfb51d1e72054c837",
